ytsearch — provenance
=====================

This crate is a clean, idiomatic rewrite of the same YouTube surface that
"yspy" (https://github.com/ityeri/yspy) scrapes, and of this repository's own
earlier line-by-line port of it ("ysrs", https://github.com/mincomk/ysrs).

yspy, Copyright (c) 2025 ityeri, is a refactored fork of the original project
"youtube-search-python" (https://github.com/alexmercerind/youtube-search-python),
Original Copyright (c) 2021 Hitesh Kumar Saini. Both are licensed under the MIT
License.

What is carried over from them:

- the innertube endpoints, client definitions and request payloads, which are
  what any client of this kind has to send;
- the JSON shapes the pages are parsed from, and the parsing rules (including
  the English-page pairing used to read abbreviated counts such as
  "573K subscribers");
- the json fixtures under tests/fixtures/, which come from yspy's test suite
  and are used here as the parsing gate.

What is new here: the public API design (a client handle, typed ids, cursor
paging, builder options), the JSON-free request/step core, and the
feature-split sync/async surfaces.

See LICENSE for the full license text that covers all of the above.
